━━━ stdout
Publish objects to intelligence platforms

␛[1m␛[4mUsage:␛[0m ␛[1mopentide share␛[0m [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

␛[1m␛[4mCommands:␛[0m
  ␛[1mpush␛[0m     Create or update one MISP event per selected object
  ␛[1mpreview␛[0m  Show what push would do, without a request
  ␛[1mstatus␛[0m   Compare the local ledger with object versions
  ␛[1mretract␛[0m  Unpublish or delete a shared event
  ␛[1mtargets␛[0m  List sharing destinations, never their API keys

␛[1m␛[4mOptions:␛[0m
      ␛[1m--target␛[0m <TARGET>
          Destination block name. Repeatable.

      ␛[1m--uuid␛[0m <UUID>
          Limit to these object UUIDs.

      ␛[1m--type␛[0m <OBJECT_TYPE>
          Limit to threat, objective, or rule.

      ␛[1m--file␛[0m <FILE>
          Limit to these object files.

      ␛[1m--dry-run␛[0m
          Resolve the run locally and make no request.

      ␛[1m--publish, --no-publish␛[0m
          Override the block publish flag.

      ␛[1m--workers␛[0m <WORKERS>
          Parallel object workers for one destination.
          
          [default: 1]

      ␛[1m--changed␛[0m
          Share only objects the default-branch CI diff changed.

      ␛[1m--since␛[0m <COMMIT>
          With --changed: diff from this commit SHA or ref to HEAD.

      ␛[1m--help␛[0m
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide share --dry-run
  $ opentide share --target misp-prod

━━━ stderr · empty
